    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_f8a11ddff7d066fd79f76ec2bff580a0400c9197732bec87c40f5af618cea284",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Continuing the random-complex-Hermitian analogy, the source proposes one determinantal form for every k-tuple correlation: a k-by-k matrix has unit diagonal and off-diagonal entries of sine-kernel type, and the preceding pair conjecture is exactly its k=2 instance. The determinant compresses pair-indexed kernel relations into a single higher-order joint law, gaining a uniform structural generalization across k, but the analogy supplies no proof and the missing display prevents safe recovery of the exact formula.",
