    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7c7efccee41cdfb3e7fd30efd0b9068930058e1b70bd7e1c1ec39f1ff011eceb",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under RH, the weighted form factor F compresses zero differences into frequency space, while the convolution identity turns a chosen local-spacing kernel into an integral of F against that kernel's Fourier profile. The proved subunit range therefore acts as an admissibility constraint on local observables: the sinc and squared-sinc choices yield concrete pair-sum asymptotics precisely because their required profiles remain inside the controlled band.",
