      "proposed_content": "The proof places a smoothed zero sum and prime-power Dirichlet sums in one explicit-formula identity L(x,t)=R(x,t), then compares their time mean squares. Expanding the zero side manufactures the pair statistic F, whereas quantitative Parseval and prime-number-theorem estimates evaluate the arithmetic side; the substitution x=T^alpha aligns scale with frequency, and a three-regime dominance analysis yields the subunit asymptotic.",
