    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f9141364c345d3f70b32f228ae415105ac4c59dedcd8c4d3607b65053d20e76b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Completing the pair form factor conjecturally produces the sine-kernel pair law, which matches the complex-Hermitian/unitary ensemble and differs from the orthogonal and symplectic form factors already distinguishable in the proved subunit range. Continuing that selected analogy then supplies a determinantal k-tuple conjecture with the pair law as its k=2 case and qualitative predictions of arbitrarily small and unbounded normalized consecutive gaps.",
